  (68, 1362, 'drug_exposure', 'increase', FALSE, 'The dose of the sensitive CYP3A substrate with a narrow therapeutic index (e.g., alfentanil, cyclosporine, dihydroergotamine, ergotamine, everolimus, fentanyl, pimozide, quinidine, sirolimus, and tacrolimus) may need to be reduced, as IBRANCE may increase its exposure [see Clinical Pharmacology (12.3) ] .'),
  (68, 1971, 'drug_exposure', 'increase', FALSE, 'Therefore, careful monitoring and/or dosage adjustment of these drugs is needed: Alfentanil (CYP3A4 substrate)– Coadministration of multiple doses of oral voriconazole (400 mg q12h on day 1, 200 mg q12h on day 2) with a single 20 mcg/kg intravenous dose of alfentanil with concomitant naloxone resulted in a 6-fold increase in mean alfentanil AUC 0-∞ and a 4-fold prolongation of mean alfentanil elimination half-life, compared to when alfentanil was given alone.'),
