  (1748, 1867, 'seizure_risk', 'unspecified', TRUE, 'Contraindicated SS Tapentadol Contraindicated HR/SS Tetrabenazine Contraindicated HR Tolcapone Use with caution HR Tramadol Use with caution SS; Increased seizure risk Tryptophan Contraindicated SS Tranylcypromine tablets inhibits intestinal MAO, which is responsible for the catabolism of tyramine in food and beverages.'),
  (1756, 1933, 'nephrotoxicity', 'increase', FALSE, '(7.2) Co-administration of piperacillin and tazobactam with vancomycin may increase the incidence of acute kidney injury.'),
